  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\integers.relation]\nDefines: R is \\equivalence.relation:on{\\naturals \\.set.cross./ \\naturals}\nexpresses:\n. forAll: n1, m1, n2, m2 is \\natural\n  then:\n  . have: R((n1, m1), (n2, m2))\n    iff: (n1 \\.natural.+./ m2) = (n2 \\.natural.+./ m1)\nDocumented:\n. called: \"integer equivalence relation\"\n. description: \"The equivalence relation on $\\mathbb{N} \\times \\mathbb{N}$\n                identifying pairs $(n_1, m_1)$ and $(n_2, m_2)$ when\n                $n_1 + m_2 = n_2 + m_1$.\"\nId: \"fd0234b9-545e-4dcf-bc4f-8c1c6f306e25\"",
